        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerakas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Gerakas sits at the junction of the Ymittos and Penteli foothills in Attica.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerakas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the ancient deme Kekropia, named after Cecrops I.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerakas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Excavations at Fouresi Hill uncovered a palaiochristian temple, proving an early Christian community existed there.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gerakas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Once a rural village of vineyards and olive groves, Gerakas has become a suburban hub while keeping its agricultural roots.",
